Equity risk is the risk of loss because of a drop in the market price of shares. 

Equity risk arises from *fluctuations in the share price* and the risk of the *issuer defaulting*.

Equity risk often refers to *equity investment risk*, which is the risk associated with the investment in shares/stocks of a company. In this case the equity risk is a #voir("specific-risk").